## 1. Product specification you must satisfy (source of truth)

The system is an **exam-lifecycle coordinator**: registration to published results, with faculty sign-off built in. It is a companion to question-paper setting: the same tagged question bank and scheme of valuation feed delivery and grading.

**Agents (each = a separately testable service module with typed input/output):**

| # | Agent | Role | Guardrail |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Coordinator | Sets up exam run, owns plan, state and audit log, drives the pipeline | Never publish without faculty approval; enforce audit logging |
| 1 | Registration & Eligibility | Checks fee status, attendance (e.g. >= 75%), prerequisite clearance | Apply rules consistently; **flag ambiguous cases for human decision** |
| 2 | Exam Delivery | Releases exam inside the delivery window, manages session access | Enforce the window; **never extend or restart a session without faculty approval** |
| 3 | Proctoring & Integrity | Monitors session activity (multiple logins, unusual timing, tab/fullscreen/audio) and flags | **Flag only; never auto-penalize or disqualify** |
| 4 | Auto-Grading (Objective) | Grades objective questions against approved answer key | Grade only against approved key; **flag key mismatches rather than guessing**; never exceed max marks |
| 5 | Subjective Grading Assist | Drafts grades vs rubric | **Draft only; never publish a subjective grade without faculty approval** |
| 6 | Grievance & Revaluation | Tracks post-result requests to resolution | **Log everything; never resolve automatically** |
| 7 | Faculty Review | Approves/adjusts integrity flags and subjective drafts | Faculty decision is final authority |
| 8 | Result Publishing & Archive | Publishes approved results, archives exam record | Full audit log of session, grading, publishing |

**Validation agent (hard gate before faculty sees results), these 4 checks must exist as code:**
1. Each candidate gets a **unique paper** (question set/order is unique per candidate and reproducible from a stored seed).
2. Integrity signals are **logged, never turned into verdicts/penalties**.
3. An auto-grade **never exceeds the maximum** marks.
4. Results are **held until faculty sign-off**.

On failure: diagnose the exact failing constraint, regenerate/repair only the failing part, bounded by `MAX_ATTEMPTS` (default 3), then escalate to faculty with a diagnosis.

**Hybrid execution:** eligibility gate and delivery window are sequential; objective grading + integrity monitoring run in parallel as submissions arrive; subjective drafting runs in parallel across students after submissions close; faculty approval and publishing are sequential gates; grievances are tracked after publish.

**Governance:** role-based access, exam confidentiality, versioned publish with **one-click rollback**, evaluation metrics, immutable audit log.

**Dashboard (faculty/CoE) must contain 4 panels:** Registration & eligibility (with flagged ambiguous cases) / Integrity report / Grading queue / Results & grievances.

**Command interface (must exist, CLI and API):**
```
/exam-agent setup-exam --course "25ECSC307" --paper "final_question_paper.docx" \
  --eligibility "fees cleared, attendance >= 75%" --delivery-window "2026-11-20 10:00-13:00" \
  --grading "objective auto-grade, subjective assisted grading" \
  --outputs "registration list, integrity report, draft grades, published results" \
  --constraints "faculty approval of subjective grades and integrity flags before publishing"
```

